<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>Run: PwnKit mitigation - Removing SUID permissions on pkexec - WITH MITIGATION</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<DIV><BR>
<P>This task will remove the SUID-bit from pkexec file.<BR>It is a generic command that can be deployed on all Linux-based endpoints <BR>chmod 0755 /usr/bin/pkexec<BR></P>
<P>You should favor patching the OS with the security update released by the vendor for any supported system, and only when this is not a viable solution, to use the mitigation approach. <BR></P>
<P><B>Removing the SUID-bit form the pkexec file may have a negative impact on any applications.<BR>Use this task to perform mitigation with care and test thoroughly in your environment.</B><BR></P></DIV>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>exists file &quot;/usr/bin/pkexec&quot; and mode of file &quot;/usr/bin/pkexec&quot; as string != &quot;rwxr-xr-x&quot;</Relevance>
    <Category>Workaround</Category>
    <Source>Community Content</Source>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2022-01-28</SourceReleaseDate>
    <SourceSeverity>Important</SourceSeverity>
    <CVENames>CVE-2021-4034</CVENames>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Tue, 01 Feb 2022 14:35:27 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to deploy this action.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">// Enter your action script here
wait &quot;/bin/bash&quot; -c &quot;chmod 0755 /usr/bin/pkexec&quot;</ActionScript>
      <SuccessCriteria Option="RunToCompletion"></SuccessCriteria>
    </DefaultAction>
  </Fixlet>
</BES>
